{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it has turned the hair white.</b> This means two hairs, and the reason that white hair is a sign of impurity is that black is the natural state of growth, and since it is white and its nature has changed, this constitutes a disease." "<b>And a quick raw flesh in the swelling.</b> This means 'or a quick raw flesh,' for it does not require both of them — white hair and raw flesh — since in the section above Scripture declares impure by white hair alone, as it is written: ״ושער בנגע הפך לבן נגע צרעת הוא וראהו הכהן וטמא אותו״, and likewise the raw flesh alone is a sign of impurity; and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived a measure for the raw flesh: that it must be large enough to receive white hair, which is two hairs." "<b>And know</b> that in every place where you find white hair [and] black hair, we follow the root of the hair: if the hair in the affliction was white but its root was black, we judge it as black; and likewise if it had black hair and the root of its root was white, we judge it as white hair."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:11.476643420Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}